column26:
*Steps:*
Insert a new transaction using a date format other than {{YYYY-MM-DD}}.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1001, 1002, 'Transfer', 500, '31-08-2026');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{1001}} exists.
* Receiver account {{1002}} exists.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1001}}
* receiver_account = {{1002}}
* transaction_type = {{Transfer}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{31-08-2026}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected because the required date format is {{YYYY-MM-DD}}.

*Steps:*
Insert a new transaction using spaces as the transaction date.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1001, 1002, 'Transfer', 500, '   ');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{1001}} exists.
* Receiver account {{1002}} exists.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1001}}
* receiver_account = {{1002}}
* transaction_type = {{Transfer}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{' '}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected because spaces are not a valid date.

*Steps:*
Insert a new transaction with an empty transaction date.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1001, 1002, 'Transfer', 500, '');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{1001}} exists.
* Receiver account {{1002}} exists.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1001}}
* receiver_account = {{1002}}
* transaction_type = {{Transfer}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{''}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected because the transaction date must be a valid date.

*Steps:*
Insert a new transaction with a NULL transaction date.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1001, 1002, 'Transfer', 500, NULL);
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{1001}} exists.
* Receiver account {{1002}} exists.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1001}}
* receiver_account = {{1002}}
* transaction_type = {{Transfer}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{NULL}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected because {{transaction_date}} is a mandatory field.

*Steps:*
Insert a new transaction using a transaction type that is not defined in the ENUM.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1001, 1002, 'Refund', 500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{1001}} exists.
* Receiver account {{1002}} exists.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1001}}
* receiver_account = {{1002}}
* transaction_type = {{Refund}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected because {{Refund}} is not an allowed ENUM value.

*Steps:*
Insert a new transaction with spaces as the transaction type.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1001, 1002, '   ', 500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{1001}} exists.
* Receiver account {{1002}} exists.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1001}}
* receiver_account = {{1002}}
* transaction_type = {{' '}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected because spaces are not a valid transaction type.

*Steps:*
Insert a new transaction with an empty transaction type.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1001, 1002, '', 500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{1001}} exists.
* Receiver account {{1002}} exists.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1001}}
* receiver_account = {{1002}}
* transaction_type = {{''}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected because the transaction type must be one of the allowed ENUM values.

*Steps:*
Insert a new transaction with a NULL transaction type.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1001, 1002, NULL, 500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{1001}} exists.
* Receiver account {{1002}} exists.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1001}}
* receiver_account = {{1002}}
* transaction_type = {{NULL}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected because {{transaction_type}} is a mandatory field.

*Steps:*
Insert a new Transfer transaction using an empty value as the receiver account.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1001, '', 'Transfer', 500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{1001}} exists.
* Sender account has sufficient balance.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1001}}
* receiver_account = {{''}}
* transaction_type = {{Transfer}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected because receiver account must contain a valid existing account number.

*Steps:*
Insert a new Transfer transaction using {{0}} as the receiver account.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1001, 0, 'Transfer', 500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{1001}} exists.
* Receiver account {{0}} does not exist.
* Sender account has sufficient balance.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1001}}
* receiver_account = {{0}}
* transaction_type = {{Transfer}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected because receiver account {{0}} does not exist in the {{Accounts}} table.

*Steps:*
Insert a new Transfer transaction using a negative receiver account.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1001, -1002, 'Transfer', 500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{1001}} exists.
* Receiver account {{-1002}} does not exist.
* Sender account has sufficient balance.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1001}}
* receiver_account = {{-1002}}
* transaction_type = {{Transfer}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected because the receiver account does not exist in the Accounts table.

*Steps:*
Insert a new Transfer transaction using a text value as the receiver account.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1001, 'ABC', 'Transfer', 500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{1001}} exists.
* Sender account has sufficient balance.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1001}}
* receiver_account = {{'ABC'}}
* transaction_type = {{Transfer}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected because {{receiver_account}} must contain a valid numeric account number.

*Steps:*
Insert a new Transfer transaction using spaces as the receiver account.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1001, '   ', 'Transfer', 500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{1001}} exists.
* Sender account has sufficient balance.
* No account exists with the specified invalid receiver value.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1001}}
* receiver_account = {{' '}}
* transaction_type = {{Transfer}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected because the receiver account must contain a valid existing account number.

*Steps:*
Insert a new Transfer transaction using a receiver account that does not exist.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1001, 9999, 'Transfer', 500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{1001}} exists.
* Receiver account {{9999}} does not exist.
* Sender account has sufficient balance.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1001}}
* receiver_account = {{9999}}
* transaction_type = {{Transfer}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected due to the Foreign Key constraint because receiver account {{9999}} does not exist.

*Steps:*
Insert a new Transfer transaction with a NULL receiver account.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1, NULL, 'Transfer', 500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{1001}} exists.
* Sender account has sufficient balance.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1}}
* receiver_account = {{NULL}}
* transaction_type = {{Transfer}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transfer transaction is rejected because a valid receiver account is required for a Transfer.

*Steps:*
Insert a new transaction using spaces as the sender account.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
('   ', 1002, 'Transfer', 500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Receiver account {{1002}} exists.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{' '}}
* receiver_account = {{1002}}
* transaction_type = {{Transfer}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected because the sender account must contain a valid existing account number.

*Steps:*
Insert a transaction using a sender account value containing spaces.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(' 1 ', 2, 'Transfer', 500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{1001}} exists.
* Receiver account {{1002}} exists.
* Sender account has sufficient balance.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{' 1 '}}
* receiver_account = {{2}}
* transaction_type = {{Transfer}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
The system should reject the transaction because {{sender_account}} should contain a valid account number without spaces.

*Steps:*
Insert a Transfer transaction using the same account as sender and receiver.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1001, 1001, 'Transfer', 500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Account {{1001}} exists.
* Account {{1001}} has sufficient balance.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1001}}
* receiver_account = {{1001}}
* transaction_type = {{Transfer}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected because a Transfer should not be performed from an account to the same account.

*Steps:*
Insert a transaction using {{0}} as the sender account

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(0, 1002, 'Transfer', 500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{0}} does not exist.
* Receiver account {{1002}} exists.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{0}}
* receiver_account = {{1002}}
* transaction_type = {{Transfer}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected because sender account {{0}} does not exist in the Accounts table.

*Steps:*
Insert a transaction using a text value as the sender account.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
('ABC', 1002, 'Transfer', 500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Receiver account {{1002}} exists.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{ABC}}
* receiver_account = {{1002}}
* transaction_type = {{Transfer}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected because {{sender_account}} is defined as an {{INT}} and must contain a valid account number.

*Steps:*
Insert a transaction using an empty value for sender account.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
('', 1002, 'Transfer', 500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Receiver account {{1002}} exists.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{''}}
* receiver_account = {{1002}}
* transaction_type = {{Transfer}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected because {{sender_account}} must contain a valid existing account number.

*Steps:*
Insert a transaction with a NULL amount.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1001, 1002, 'Transfer', NULL, '2026-08-31');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{1001}} exists.
* Receiver account {{1002}} exists.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1001}}
* receiver_account = {{1002}}
* transaction_type = {{Transfer}}
* amount = {{NULL}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected because amount is mandatory and must be greater than zero.

*Steps:*
Insert a transaction with a NULL transaction type.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1001, 1002, NULL, 500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{1001}} exists.
* Receiver account {{1002}} exists.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1001}}
* receiver_account = {{1002}}
* transaction_type = {{NULL}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected because {{transaction_type}} is mandatory.

*Steps:*
Insert a transaction with a negative amount.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1001, 1002, 'Transfer', -500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{1001}} exists.
* Receiver account {{1002}} exists.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1001}}
* receiver_account = {{1002}}
* transaction_type = {{Transfer}}
* amount = {{-500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected because the amount must be greater than zero.

*Steps:*
Insert a transaction with amount equal to zero.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1001, 1002, 'Transfer', 0, '2026-08-31');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{1001}} exists.
* Receiver account {{1002}} exists.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1001}}
* receiver_account = {{1002}}
* transaction_type = {{Transfer}}
* amount = {{0}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is rejected because the amount must be greater than zero.

*Steps:*
Insert a Transfer transaction within the daily transfer limit.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1001, 1002, 'Transfer', 35000, '2026-08-31');
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Daily transfer limit = {{40000}}.
* Sender account {{1001}} exists.
* Receiver account {{1002}} exists.
* Sender has sufficient balance.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1001}}
* receiver_account = {{1002}}
* transaction_type = {{Transfer}}
* amount = {{35000}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transfer is created successfully because the total daily transfer amount does not exceed the configured daily limit.

*Steps:*
Attempt to create a Withdrawal transaction exceeding the available balance.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1001, NULL, 'Withdrawal', 1500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

Verify the account balance:

{code:sql}SELECT account_number, balance
FROM Accounts
WHERE account_number = 1001;
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Account {{1001}} exists.
* Current balance = {{1000}}.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1001}}
* receiver_account = {{NULL}}
* transaction_type = {{Withdrawal}}
* amount = {{1500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*

* Transaction fails.
* Account balance remains {{1000}}.
* No amount is deducted from the account.

*Steps:*
Insert a valid Transfer transaction.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1, 2, 'Transfer', 500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

Verify both account balances:

{code:sql}SELECT account_number, balance
FROM Accounts
WHERE account_number IN (1, 2);
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Sender account {{1}} exists with balance {{1000}}.
* Receiver account {{2}} exists with balance {{2000}}.
* Sender has sufficient balance.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1}}
* receiver_account = {{2}}
* transaction_type = {{Transfer}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*

* Transfer is created successfully.
* Sender balance changes from {{1000}} to {{500}}.
* Receiver balance changes from {{2000}} to {{2500}}.
* Both balance updates occur as one atomic operation.

*Steps:*
Insert a valid Withdrawal transaction.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1, NULL, 'Withdrawal', 500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

Verify the account balance:

{code:sql}SELECT account_number, balance
FROM Accounts
WHERE account_number = 1;
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Account {{1}} exists.
* Current balance = {{1000}}.
* Account has sufficient balance.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1}}
* receiver_account = {{NULL}}
* transaction_type = {{Withdrawal}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is created successfully and the account balance is automatically updated from {{1000}} to {{500}}.

*Steps:*
Insert a valid Deposit transaction.

{code:sql}INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1, NULL, 'Deposit', 500, '2026-08-31');
{code}

Verify the account balance:

{code:sql}SELECT account_number, balance
FROM Accounts
WHERE account_number = 1;
{code}

*Preconditions:*

* Account {{1}} exists.
* Current balance = {{1000}}.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1}}
* receiver_account = {{NULL}}
* transaction_type = {{Deposit}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Transaction is created successfully and the account balance is automatically updated from {{1000}} to {{1500}}.

*Steps:*
Insert a Withdrawal transaction with an amount greater than the sender account balance.

* INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1, NULL, 'Withdrawal', 1500, '2026-08-31');

*Preconditions:*

* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{1}} exists.
* Sender account balance is {{1000}}.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1}}
* receiver_account = {{NULL}}
* transaction_type = {{Withdrawal}}
* amount = {{1500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Withdrawal transaction is rejected because the withdrawal amount exceeds the available balance, and the account balance remains unchanged.

*Steps:*
Insert a new Deposit transaction with a NULL receiver account.

* INSERT INTO Transactions
(sender_account, receiver_account, transaction_type, amount, transaction_date)
VALUES
(1001, NULL, 'Deposit', 500, '2026-08-31');



* *Preconditions:*
* Transactions table exists.
* Sender account {{1}} exists.
* Deposit transactions allow a NULL receiver account.

*Test Data:*

* sender_account = {{1}}
* receiver_account = {{NULL}}
* transaction_type = {{Deposit}}
* amount = {{500}}
* transaction_date = {{2026-08-31}}

*Test Environment:*
MySQL

*Expected Result:*
Deposit transaction is created successfully with {{receiver_account}} set to NULL.
